<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Trafalgar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1805">1805</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Trafalgar was a naval battle fought in 1805 off Cape Trafalgar in southwestern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, in which the British fleet under Admiral Nelson defeated the combined fleets of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and Spain. Nelson was killed during the battle. The victory established British naval supremacy for the next century, a foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>'s global power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-trafalgar.jpg" alt="Battle of Trafalgar" width="320" height="184" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Clarkson Frederick Stanfield · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Battle_of_Trafalgar_by_William_Clarkson_Stanfield.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
